{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Air Raid Siren",
 "category": "Effects",
 "text": "Sound: a slow, wailing air-raid siren rising and falling, far away across a city.\n\nHow it's built: a triangle LFO, very slow, into an oscillator's FM at a full octave: the pitch climbs and falls over about three seconds. A sine and a square mixed for a hollow, mechanical tone; a big Reverb for distance.\n\nPlay: hold one note (the low point of the wail).\n\nTweak: the LFO's RATE, the oscillator's FM, the reverb's MIX.",
